---
layout: base.njk
title: Follow the journal
description: Receive quiet notifications directly on your device when a new page is published, or follow via email or feed reader.
section: subscribe
permalink: /subscribe/
---
<section class="subscribe-page">
  <div class="subscribe-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span>NOTES FROM THE MARGINS</p>
    <h1>A new page,<br><em>occasionally.</em></h1>
    <p class="subscribe-intro">No schedule, no noise, no endless inbox newsletters. Get a quiet notification directly on your phone or computer screen whenever another page is written.</p>

    <!-- Web Push Primary Card -->
    <div class="push-card" data-notification-card>
      <div class="push-card-header">
        <span class="push-badge"><span class="push-dot"></span> IN-APP & DEVICE PUSH</span>
        <span class="push-tag">Instant · Private</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Direct to your screen.</h2>
      <p class="push-desc">Receive a calm ping on your phone lock screen or desktop notification center. No email address required, no spam, and zero tracking.</p>

      <div class="push-action-row">
        <button class="primary-button push-toggle-btn" type="button" data-notification-btn aria-live="polite">
          <span class="push-btn-icon" aria-hidden="true">✦</span>
          <span data-notification-label>Enable device notifications</span>
        </button>
        <span class="push-support-hint" data-notification-status>Supports Chrome, Safari, Edge, Firefox, and mobile PWAs.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="push-test-row" data-notification-test-row hidden>
        <button class="ghost-button push-test-btn" type="button" data-notification-test-btn>Send test notification ↗</button>
        <button class="ghost-button push-disable-btn" type="button" data-notification-disable-btn>Turn off notifications</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Secondary Alternatives -->
    <div class="alt-options">
      <span class="small-label">OTHER WAYS TO FOLLOW</span>
      <div class="alt-options-grid">
        <div class="alt-card">
          <h3>Occasional email</h3>
          <p>If you still prefer an email note, finish signing up securely on Buttondown.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ site.newsletter.url }}">Continue to email signup <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="alt-card">
          <h3>Feed reader</h3>
          <p>Follow the Atom XML feed in NetNewsWire, Feedly, or your reader of choice.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="{{ '/feed.xml' | url }}">Open the journal feed <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="subscribe-aside" aria-label="What to expect">
    <span class="small-label">WHAT TO EXPECT</span>
    <ul class="subscribe-promises">
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <p><strong>Zero inbox clutter.</strong> Direct to your device without getting lost in promotions or spam.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <p><strong>Total privacy.</strong> We never collect, store, or sell your personal details or email address.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <p><strong>You’re in control.</strong> Toggle notifications off at any time with a single tap.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="install-card" data-install-card hidden>
      <span class="small-label">INSTALL TO HOME SCREEN</span>
      <p>Add <em>In the margins</em> to your home screen or dock to read like a standalone app.</p>
      <button class="ghost-button install-btn" type="button" data-install-btn>Add to home screen ↗</button>
    </div>
  </aside>
</section>

